  "body": "Asked for by the maintainer in chat, 2026-11-17:\n\n> \"we should be able to \"Save\" panel setups what is opened, where they are attached and how.\"\n\nThe maintainer set the priority `P3` in the same message.\n\nWhat is wanted: the user can save the panel setup of the window and get it back later. A saved panel setup holds:\n\n- which panels are open;\n- where each panel is attached (the dock side or area, or a floating window with its position);\n- how each panel is attached (its size, its tab order, its collapsed state).\n\nToday: the user arranges the panels by hand. The application has no command to save an arrangement or to load one.\n\nOpen points for the worker (record each choice in `docs/decisions/`):\n\n- one saved setup, or several named setups;\n- where the setup is stored (the application settings, not the project file, is the recommended default);\n- whether the last arrangement loads automatically at the next start;\n- a \"reset to default\" command.\n\nRules that apply: a change from the UI is a command (AGENTS.md \"Everything Is a Command\"); a panel arrangement is UI state, thus decide and record whether it is undoable. A corrupt or old saved setup must load the default arrangement with a diagnostic. It must not crash.\n\nDone means: the user saves a panel setup, changes the arrangement, loads the saved setup, and gets the saved arrangement again, also after a restart. A test in the structural suite pins the round trip (open panels, attachment, size).\n",
